1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:02,060
PS5 games on a PC,

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:03,220
with no emulator.

3
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:05,220
This free tool rewrites the game itself

4
00:00:05,240 --> 00:00:06,600
into a Windows program.

5
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:09,040
The PS5's processor already speaks your

6
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:10,300
PC's language.

7
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:12,340
It just swaps in its own versions of

8
00:00:12,360 --> 00:00:14,150
Sony's system libraries.

9
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:16,120
One game works so far:

10
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:20,480
60 frames per second on a GTX 1050 Ti.

11
00:00:20,620 --> 00:00:23,740
16,000 GitHub stars in two months.

12
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:26,300
It's called AnyPS5.

13
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:27,550
Bring your own games,

14
00:00:27,570 --> 00:00:29,640
and only download it from GitHub.
